# LUMEN — Always-on rules

## Stack (mandatory)
- Tauri v2 (Rust) + React 18 + Vite + TypeScript **strict**.
- Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui; zustand; @tanstack/react-query; framer-motion;
  lucide-react; react-virtuoso; SQLite via tauri-plugin-sql.
- Inter + JetBrains Mono bundled locally — never CDN.
- Rust does ONLY: fs walk, watch, volumes info, db, cache file io, open-external,
  single-instance, associations, bundling.
- Thumbnails + metadata extracted on the frontend (webp 480w → appCacheDir/thumbs,
  4-worker queue; exifreader for images). No ffmpeg sidecar in v1.

## Design tokens (v2 soft glass editorial — full spec in docs/DESIGN.md)
- Canvas #0A0A0C; surface-1 #141518; surface-2 #1E2023; surface-3 #26282C.
- Tonal elevation over borders; hairlines only as editorial dividers.
- Glass (topbar/sidebar/floating/menus): white 5% + blur(28) saturate(1.2)
  + inner top highlight white/6.
- Radii: card 22, control 14, viewer 16, pill 999.
- Chunky controls: buttons h44/48, icon buttons 40, inputs 44, menu items 40, FAB 56.
- Air: card padding 24-28, grid gap 12-16, sidebar rows 44-48, gutters 32-40,
  section rhythm 48-64.
- Type: display 28-40/650; section 18-20/600; body 14-15/400 lh 1.55.
  Mono ONLY for metadata/counters/timecodes/paths. Max 1-2 mono micro-labels
  per screen; oversized thin accent section numbers ("01", 300).
- Text #F2F2F4 / 62% / 38%. Accent #6EC1FF — interactive + progress ONLY.
- success #3ECF8E, danger #FF5C5C, warning #F5B85C.
- Elevation: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.35); dialogs 0 12px 32px .55.
- Hover: lift -2px + soft shadow + accent glow; pressed scale .97.
- framer-motion springs 260/26; route cross-fade 180ms; prefers-reduced-motion.
- Focus-visible 2px accent/40 offset 2. Scrollbars 8px thumb white/12→/20.
- 2% grain overlay; vignette only in viewers. Inter + JetBrains Mono local only.

## Process
- **Re-read docs/DESIGN.md before ANY UI work.**
- **Run typecheck (`tsc --noEmit`) + `cargo clippy` before every commit.**
- **Checkpoint commit after EVERY completed checklist item** (`chore: checkpoint ...`)
  so a stream drop never loses more than one step.
- **Never guess Tauri v2 permission names**; verify against plugin docs or the
  expected-list printed in build errors.
- Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `chore:`, etc.
- CLEAN SHUTDOWN: track PIDs of every background process started; at end of session kill each with taskkill /T /PID; verify ports 1420/1421 free (Get-NetTCPConnection) and no project node.exe/lumen.exe/cargo processes remain (Get-CimInstance Win32_Process filtered by CommandLine); never leave dev servers running — verification is typecheck + clippy + cargo check, user runs the app manually for screenshots.
- After rewriting any page component, re-verify its primary user journey (onClick -> api -> command -> state transition) before commit; all invoke errors must be surfaced (console + toast); user click-through required before phase acceptance.
  One conventional commit per phase (checkpoints are `chore:` and allowed in addition).
- After every UI phase: run dev server, screenshot, self-review token-by-token
  against docs/DESIGN.md, fix discrepancies BEFORE committing.
- Offline-first: zero network, zero telemetry. All state in SQLite.
- Work phase-by-phase per TODO.md; docs in docs/ are source of truth.

DISK GUARD — HARD RULE:
- NEVER run `cargo test`, `cargo build --release`, or any command expected to write >500 MB without explicit user approval first.
- Before ANY heavy Rust operation, check disk space: `Get-PSDrive C | Select-Object Free`.
- If free space <20 GB, STOP and ask user; suggest `cargo clean --profile release` or skipping tests.
- `pnpm tauri dev` is allowed (incremental, ~1-2 GB).
- `cargo check` and `cargo clippy` are allowed (no full linking).
- Log disk usage before/after heavy operations.